#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Availability Heuristic 🧠]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Mental shortcut for estimating likelihood 🎰]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Based on ease of recall 📝]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Can lead to biases 🙈]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("The availability heuristic is a mental shortcut we use to estimate the likelihood or frequency of events.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("It's based on how easily examples of such events come to mind. The easier it is to recall or imagine instances of an event, the more likely we perceive it to be.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("However, this can lead to biases, as the availability of examples in our memory doesn't always reflect the true probability of an event.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Example: Shark Attacks 🦈]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Extensive media coverage 📰]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Easily recalled 🧠]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Overestimation of risk 📈]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("For instance, shark attacks often receive extensive media coverage.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Because of this, examples of shark attacks are easily recalled.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("As a result, people tend to overestimate the risk of a shark attack, even though the actual probability is quite low.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Example: Lottery Wins 🎉]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Highly publicized 📣]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Readily available in memory 🧠]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Overestimation of chances 📈]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Similarly, lottery wins are often highly publicized.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("This makes instances of people winning the lottery readily available in our memory.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Consequently, people tend to overestimate their chances of winning, despite the odds being extremely low.")
]
]

#slide()[
